	(global_label "VSYS" (shape bidirectional) (at 441.96 149.86 270) (fields_autoplaced yes) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify right)) (uuid "8b92aaf7-989e-509d-b32f-ae38f8062ded") (property "Intersheetrefs" "${INTERSHEET_REFS}" (at 441.96 149.86 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (hide yes))))
	(text "USB-C input, charger, fuel gauge, 5 V boost" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 15.24 0) (effects (font (size 3.0 3.0)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a816b872-f3e7-5630-b13a-b97c567f052e"))
	(text "USB-C: sink only, 5.1k Rd on CC1/CC2 (no PD controller). BQ25895 typical application (TI SLUSC88C Fig. 9-1)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 21.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "83dd8681-5b19-5735-86d9-42ad9aa7db00"))
	(text "P1: the BQ25895 asks HVDCP/MaxCharge adapters for 9-12 V by default (REG02 reset values). R21/R22 are DNP," (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 25.44 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "9f4ac57a-4884-5c5c-a028-1e48dc0cdbae"))
	(text "    so the charger never sees D+/D-: VBUS stays at 5 V and the input limit resets to 500 mA. VBUS parts are" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 29.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "e8afbe01-9401-5b67-ab1e-56d5865056e5"))
	(text "    D5 is a 6 V stand-off TVS (clamps near 10 V, under the charger VBUS limit of 22 V): if R21/R22 are ever" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 33.84 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "0bb2a217-7eeb-5138-a63a-4ab795ab0c30"))
	(text "    fitted for 9-12 V input it must be changed with them." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 38.04 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "2a9b5172-7632-5ccd-a2ee-5b611ae1bf9f"))
	(text "P3: ILIM 470R caps the input at 0.68/0.755/0.83 A, with \"ti,use-ilim-pin\" in the device tree (the reset state)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 42.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "2bb0bbd0-aa6e-53f7-9e77-72930ae867c8"))
	(text "P7: the charger resets to 2.048 A charge current and the pack allows 1.4 A. With the 500 mA input default" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 46.44 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "62f87c6f-c921-5fe7-841a-fa676995da60"))
	(text "    the pack sees about 0.6 A until Linux sets \"ti,charge-current\" (1.4 A or less)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 50.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "b124bd2d-bb39-5fe1-bdf8-f178c7295140"))
	(text "Cell: BAK LP-454965-2P-3M pack, 2800 mAh min, 5.6 A max discharge, 1.4 A max charge, 10k NTC (David 2026-11-24)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 54.84 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "c4b1e08e-521e-5b2a-9b7a-94831a194858"))
	(text "REQUIRED (David 2026-11-24): never draw the cell above its rating (5.6 A). U13, a TPS259571 eFuse with RILM 680R," (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 59.04 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "6a953543-826b-5d78-860e-8d5ff1587100"))
	(text "    limits everything fed from VSYS_LIM (the 5 V boost and the backlight) to about 3.0 A (David 2026-11-25: fuse" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 63.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "449c92ab-3d95-58b4-9fed-37cb174b54e9"))
	(text "    instead of the 1.7 A TPS2553). 3.0 A is also the rating of the battery connector with 22 AWG leads." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 67.44 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a8cadcc2-85e1-593f-8f43-1633ff62200f"))
	(text "    When it limits, VSYS_LIM sags, the boost under-voltage divider turns the 5 V rail off, and FLT tells the module." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 71.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "849e4e58-10ab-5e00-8c2f-37d06a680abf"))
	(text "Hard power-cycle option (David 2026-11-25), all DNP: with C90, R91 and D9 fitted, holding the power button pulls" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 75.84 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "f691c0d6-120d-5c2a-94c8-391c4a59d260"))
	(text "    FUSE_EN down through 1M; after about 3 s (1.2 x R91 x C90) it passes 1.1 V and U13 cuts VSYS_LIM, so the module" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 80.04 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "1c7c3e47-784a-533a-a7af-ea08a2e94097"))
	(text "    loses 5 V. After release R90 charges C90 again and power returns in about 8 s. For a module that cannot be" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 84.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "55aa67ef-f02b-557c-a1b5-aaf4811d6a57"))
	(text "    woken after poweroff. Values are a starting point; without these parts the fuse is simply always on." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 88.44 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "08486c1d-5d21-512e-b601-8a2a3cfb75e8"))
	(text "Fuel gauge MAX17048 (voltage-only, no sense resistor): CELL/VDD taken as a Kelvin tap from the cell + pad." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 92.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "e80824ca-da9c-5799-9f11-7f8ecfeb074f"))
	(text "Boost TPS61230: VOUT = 1 V x (1 + 402k/100k) = 5.02 V (TI SLVSAQ2C 9.2.1.2.1)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 96.84 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "d23d002e-654a-5a28-be84-3a001c50ef15"))
	(text "P5: EN/HYS divider 1M / 560k / 51k -> boost on above VSYS 3.31 V, off below 3.01 V (SLVSAQ2C 8.3.4, eq. 3)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 101.04 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "1865d0a7-9b46-544a-b34a-d5c5acf78b38"))
	(text "M1/P6: power button SW1 pulls three isolated nodes low through D3/D7/D8: charger /QON (ship-mode exit," (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 105.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "80a757ca-4513-5eaa-b44f-d65225b03518"))
	(text "    12-18 s hold = battery FET reset), module pin 99 through 1k, and a plain GPIO power key (pin 41)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 109.44 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "3afa8c9f-8051-50a3-8a3b-d2f1793f2de0"))
	(text "    Core3566 pin 99 is documented as an OUTPUT: TODO(verify) on a real module before trusting it." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 113.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "ee34f704-8dc2-541d-a467-59f2c4ed88b1"))
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
